{"title":"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which is the largest sum?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb62b41058929ab4aa22964181dabe45e1b315b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"584\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28very_slow.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(very_slow)\">Solution 1 (very slow)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (very slow)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can convert each fraction to a common denominator in multiple steps, and compare the numerators to see which one is the largest.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1331db46d2cf4e7d3def7bb263c36cced6590e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{1 \\times 5}{4 \\times 5} + \\frac{1 \\times 4}{5 \\times 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"185\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e5442626b4d79b692b8e7d21914d59050333d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{5}{20} + \\frac{4}{20} = \\frac{5 + 4}{20} = \\frac{9}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfb85a0823133ab074f3b383d8592807f908934c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} + \\frac{1 \\times 2}{6 \\times 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"185\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed998c3d4174a3f8d7aed81865ac6523e6aaf2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{3}{12} + \\frac{2}{12} = \\frac{3 + 2}{12} = \\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57db9a638a20c5fb26d6a47bf51a6d031d6d8f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} + \\frac{1 \\times 4}{3 \\times 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"185\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/670acb0a167d62b778e654bd433db03de51fb066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{3}{12} + \\frac{4}{12} = \\frac{3 + 4}{12} = \\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" />. This has a larger numerator than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939c008e45e53866b9a3b3fc78db67c42d473aad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />, so it must be the larger value. This means that we don't have to include <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939c008e45e53866b9a3b3fc78db67c42d473aad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> in our comparison from now on.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351c81005b2cd18d006f727b9b99f2e5dda604d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{1 \\times 2}{4 \\times 2} + \\frac{1 \\times 1}{8 \\times 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"185\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f822df595864a749c5d93f1ce557a8210d17ba2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2}{8} + \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{2 + 1}{8} = \\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"175\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423fc422cfd9faf08898de86e2023f45d1474afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{7} = \\frac{1 \\times 7}{4 \\times 7} + \\frac{1 \\times 4}{7 \\times 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"185\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f71d9e4e6669a55d54d2f834e95702a77ae4b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{7}{28} + \\frac{4}{28} = \\frac{7 + 4}{28} = \\frac{11}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We can now compare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb2a4624c9d56c651bd76aa7359c2d4cb653bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a2370a3e7c4737d9b84d5546ce132105975dc476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> using a common denominator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8f5c76a291d4cd9b200b9e05e4c77262169837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{20} = \\frac{9 \\times 3}{20 \\times 3} = \\frac{27}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e0634ec703f5250eb8fbea7fc6348262b456af20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} = \\frac{7 \\times 5}{12 \\times 5} = \\frac{35}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />. This has the larger numerator here with the same denominator, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/978de272fb55e790150b8d4f8fbbacf5f0c6927e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e6712ed0f56b5c6e9094e35236fed92e318da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We can now compare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a2370a3e7c4737d9b84d5546ce132105975dc476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639534d18207fde5d468bcf2bb90aa2d7ad517ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> using a common denominator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13232df5a3859594c2cfbe630161e2f2fdb324c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} = \\frac{7 \\times 2}{12 \\times 2} = \\frac{14}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358922d6057d7769f85108f0529bb1f6a481e878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{3 \\times 3}{8 \\times 3} = \\frac{9}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />. This has the smaller numerator with the same denominator, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/978de272fb55e790150b8d4f8fbbacf5f0c6927e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85c22a702496ac161cb5ae98fe6a7109f266882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We can now compare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a2370a3e7c4737d9b84d5546ce132105975dc476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee525b71ec7bb581b2b7e854ab132a3de238e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad5471008199a9673d13fc6a35debaac099df69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} = \\frac{7 \\times 7}{12 \\times 7} = \\frac{49}{84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e33bc12b4cc08b8c71de656a527db9df3f93eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{28} = \\frac{11 \\times 3}{28 \\times 3} = \\frac{33}{84}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />. This has the smaller numerator with the same denominator, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/978de272fb55e790150b8d4f8fbbacf5f0c6927e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b580955cd867fbd3c1734f9ecbe34fb21e688a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Because all of the other answer choices have been eliminated, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11fd1bbcd2b1ed2f5a56b1fe6da2141ed78110ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"97\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(faster)\">Solution 2 (faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without converting to like-terms and adding the fractions, we can simply compare the denominators and see which answer choice has the smallest denominator to find the largest sum. All of the answer choices contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so that part doesn't matter. However, each one of the answer choices has a different fraction that has the same numerator but different denominators.\n</p><p>The answer choice with the smallest denominator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11fd1bbcd2b1ed2f5a56b1fe6da2141ed78110ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"97\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017223331\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.111 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 255/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2329/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 589/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/